findings.body:
`WryWebviewDispatcher::delete_cookie` now sends `WebviewMessage::SetCookie`, so `Webview::delete_cookie` and `WebviewWindow::delete_cookie` write the cookie instead of removing it. The event loop handler at `crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs:3731-3740` routes `SetCookie` to `webview.set_cookie`, so no path in this change deletes a cookie.

The intent was to remove the redundant `.clone()`, and that only needs `DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned())`. The variant should stay as it was. `set_cookie` directly above has the same shape and correctly uses `SetCookie`, so this looks like a copy-paste from it. Commit `e384526` in this repo's history, which has the same title, keeps `DeleteCookie` and changes only the clone.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1720"}

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718-1718"}
        WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

The public `Webview::delete_cookie` in `crates/tauri/src/webview/mod.rs` (around line 2097) delegates straight to this method, so every caller is affected.

`created_window_count` is declared `let mut`, but `fetch_add` takes `&self`, so `mut` is never needed. rustc reports `unused_mut` for this. The lint job runs `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, which would reject the warning if `examples/api` is part of that workspace.

The `let mut` was already in the base. The PR moves it into the new desktop-only block, so it is a good time to drop the `mut`.

